<title>USA: U.S. Sept T-bonds extend losses to one full point.</title>
<headline>U.S. Sept T-bonds extend losses to one full point.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. September Treasury bond futures were more than one full point lower in early trading, reaching a five-week low at 113-4/2.</p>
<p>Traders said trade was brisk, with widespread liquidation seen in the pits. They blamed the slide on technical followthrough from losses late Thursday.</p>
<p>More support was pegged at 112-29/32, the 50-day average.</p>
<p>((Chicago Derivatives Desk 312-408-8750))</p>
